/*
    `=>` denotes a function. It is left-declarative: it introduces one new scope frame
    that is declarative in the left operand (the pattern) and referential in the right
    operand (the body).
    So `x` is declared by the pattern and merely referred to in the body.
    `int x` is not a type annotation: `int` is a SET, and the pattern says `x` is a
    member of it.
*/

int x => x * 2
